🎯 Number Guessing Game

A beginner-friendly Python command-line game where the computer randomly chooses a number between 1 and 100, and the player tries to guess it.
After every guess, the program tells the player whether the guess is too high, too low, or correct.
The game also includes a maximum of 7 attempts and gives the player the option to play again after the game ends.


📌 Features
🎲 Generates a random number between 1 and 100
🔢 Allows the user to enter guesses
⬆️ Tells the user when the guess is too high
⬇️ Tells the user when the guess is too low
✅ Detects when the correct number is guessed
🔢 Counts the number of attempts
⏳ Limits the player to 7 attempts
💀 Displays "Game Over" when all attempts are used
🔄 Allows the player to play again
🚪 Allows the user to exit using n or q
