🎯 Maximum 7 Attempts

The program keeps track of attempts using:

attempt = 0

Every time the user makes a guess:

attempt += 1

The program then checks how many attempts remain:

if attempt < 7:
    print(f"You have only {7-attempt} attempts")
else:
    print("Game over")

This gives the player a maximum of 7 guesses.


💀 Game Over

If the player fails to guess the number within 7 attempts, the game ends.

Example:

Enter your guess: 90
Too high!

+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++

Game over

+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++



🔄 Play Again Feature

After the game ends, the program asks:

If you want to play again(y/n):

If the player enters:

y

the game starts again with a new random number.

If the player enters:

n

the program displays:

Bye

and exits.


The program uses continue to start another game:

if play == "y" or play == "Y":
    continue


🚪 Quit Option

The player can also enter:

q

when asked for a guess.


This immediately breaks out of the current guessing loop.


